design.daemon_changes:
Two Go changes, both android-only, shipped as patches regenerated with appctr/patches/recreate_patches.sh (it already diffs router_linux.go into patch 13; add one line for patch 16: `diff -u orig/net/netns/netns_android.go tailscale_src/net/netns/netns_android.go > patches/16-android-somark.patch || true` — the empty-patch guard covers it). build.sh applies with -F0, so edit tailscale_src and regenerate rather than hand-editing patch files.

A. NEW patches/16-android-somark.patch — net/netns/netns_android.go. Today UseSocketMark() hard-returns false (:25-28) and controlC (:72-108) only invokes the two JNI hooks, which are nil in this tree. Add (imports: log, net, os, golang.org/x/sys/unix):
  // TailsocksBypassMark is set with SO_MARK on every socket tailscaled opens itself when it runs as root
  // (TailSocks Root Mode). TailSocks installs `ip rule add fwmark 0x0/0x2000000 iif lo lookup 52 priority 200`,
  // so unmarked packets consult the daemon's table (peer routes, exit-node default) and marked ones fall
  // through to netd's own rules. Bit 25 is outside Android's Fwmark layout (bits 0-20) and distinct from
  // TailSocks' bit 24 (0x1000000).
  const TailsocksBypassMark = 0x2000000
  var socketMarkOnce struct { sync.Once; ok bool }
  func socketMarkWorks() bool {
      socketMarkOnce.Do(func() {
          if os.Getuid() != 0 { return }              // needs CAP_NET_ADMIN; the JNI hooks cover the app-VPN case
          c, err := net.DialUDP("udp", nil, &net.UDPAddr{IP: net.IPv4(127,0,0,1), Port: 1}); if err != nil { return }
          defer c.Close()
          rc, err := c.SyscallConn(); if err != nil { return }
          var serr error
          if err := rc.Control(func(fd uintptr) { serr = setBypassMark(int(fd)) }); err != nil || serr != nil {
              log.Printf("netns: SO_MARK %#x on tailscaled sockets unavailable (%v %v); exit nodes in Root Mode will loop", TailsocksBypassMark, err, serr); return
          }
          socketMarkOnce.ok = true
          log.Printf("netns: SO_MARK %#x set on tailscaled sockets (root bypass)", TailsocksBypassMark)
      })
      return socketMarkOnce.ok
  }
  func setBypassMark(fd int) error { if err := unix.SetsockoptInt(fd, unix.SOL_SOCKET, unix.SO_MARK, TailsocksBypassMark); err != nil { return fmt.Errorf("setting SO_MARK bypass: %w", err) }; return nil }
  func UseSocketMark() bool { return socketMarkWorks() }
  In controlC, first statement inside the c.Control closure:
      if socketMarkWorks() { if err := setBypassMark(fdInt); err != nil { sockErr = err; return } }
  Keep androidProtectFunc/androidBindToNetworkFunc unchanged. Do NOT flip netns_linux.go's build tag instead: its bindToDevice fallback (netns_linux.go:120-133) uses netmon.DefaultRouteInterface(), which on android returns the never-set lastKnownDefaultRouteIfName, so a failed SO_MARK would bind every socket to 'lo'.
  Which sockets get marked (netns.Listener/NewDialer/FromDialer attach control(), netns.go:90-130): magicsock UDP (magicsock.go:3712, 4082), DERP (derphttp_client.go:612,714), control plane and every tsdial.SystemDial user (tsdial.go:538-541), netcheck/STUN (netcheck.go:895,1201), dnsfallback (dnsfallback.go:136), DoH/TCP DNS upstreams (forwarder.go:994). Deliberately NOT marked, so they follow the exit node like any app: peerapi/exit-node-DoH dials to tailnet IPs (tsdial.dialPeerAPI -> plain net.Dialer, PeerDialControlFunc nil on android), the DNS forwarder's UDP upstream (stdNetPacketListener, forwarder.go:504-512), SOCKS/HTTP-proxy user dials (tsdial.go:598-616). LocalAPI is a unix socket; loopback dials (ByeDPI control proxy) are decided by the local table at pref 0 regardless of mark.

B. UPDATE patches/13-android-osrouter.patch — wgengine/router/osrouter/router_linux.go (keep the existing '!android' -> 'linux' tag flip and the two netmon files unchanged; add import "runtime"). Four small android gates:
  1. platformCanNetfilter() (:1924-1935): `if runtime.GOOS == "android" { return false }` with a comment (netd owns netfilter; Tailscale's 0x40000/0x80000/0xff0000 are netd's permission bits; the nft nat chain type is missing on WSA; TailSocks installs its own iptables rules). Effect: setNetfilterModeLocked forces mode Off (:746-748) so AddChains/AddHooks/AddBase/CGNAT/connmark/SNAT/stateful never run (all already gated on netfilterMode: :573-599, :1158, :1809, :1822, :1835), Set() returns nil -> SetRouterHealth(nil) clears the 'router' warning (userspace.go:899), and cleanUp() at daemon start (:1940-1949) skips the netfilter cleanups. nfr is still created (setupNetfilterLocked -> linuxfw.New -> nftables.New() is lazy and does not touch the kernel; CheckIPv6 is a netlink RuleList), so getV6Available (:922-933) keeps working and IPv6 addresses/routes are still installed. Close()'s DelConnmarkSaveRule (:396) then only logs a warning.
  2. ipRules() (:1651-1656): `if runtime.GOOS == "android" { return nil }` — no 5210/5230/5250/5270 on Android (main/default are empty there; the app's pref-200 rule replaces 5270). justAddIPRules (:1659) and the netmon-driven restore (:345-368) become no-ops.
  3. delIPRules() (:1736-1771): iterate a new ipRulesToDelete() that returns baseIPRules on android and ipRules() elsewhere, so Up() -> addIPRules() -> delIPRules() purges the desktop rules left by a previous TailSocks core (RuleDel by priority/table/type with Mark/Mask=-1, ENOENT ignored). In addIPRules() (:1505-1517) make a delIPRules error non-fatal on android (r.logf and continue) so a purge failure can never abort router.Up (userspace.go:557-559 would otherwise kill the daemon).
  4. After the RuleList probe (:157-167): `if runtime.GOOS == "android" && !r.ipRuleAvailable { r.logf("android: policy-routing probe failed; using table %d anyway (TailSocks owns the ip rules)", tailscaleRouteTable.Num); r.ipRuleAvailable = true }` so routes always go to table 52 (routeTable :1375-1380) and throw routes are installed (:1213-1215) — this also closes the table-0 hypothesis by construction.
  Everything else stays: LinkSetUp (:1382-1392), AddrReplace/AddrDel + orphan sweep (:994-1048, :483-517), RouteReplace into 52 (:1190-1206), RTN_THROW for LocalRoutes (:1212-1231), delRoutes on Close. ConsolidatingRoutes (userspace.go:347-361) keeps wrapping it on android.

Not needed / not recommended: PATCHing {"NetfilterMode":0,"NetfilterModeSet":true} via appctr.PatchPrefsJSON works too, but only after the app connects and not for cleanUp() — the Go gate covers boot-script starts. Do not remove ts_omit_iptables. Never set TS_DEBUG_FIREWALL_MODE on this binary. appctr/appctr.go:385-412 (OverrideDNSResolvers) is dead code; delete it in a separate commit. TS_DNS_FALLBACK (patch 11, set by RootUtils.kt:188-189 and tailscaled.sh:57) must stay mandatory in Root Mode.
